    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.files\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI want to navigate to currently editing buffer path while mini.files is open and using `cwd` as anchor. \r\n\r\nI tried this,\r\n\r\n```\r\n...\r\n  local navigate_to_cwd = function()\r\n    buffers = vim.api.nvim_command_output(\"ls t\")\r\n    cbuf = tonumber(string.match(buffers, '%d+'))\r\n    MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(cbuf))\r\n  end\r\n...\r\n  vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n    pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\r\n    callback = function(args)\r\n      local buf_id = args.data.buf_id\r\n      vim.keymap.set('n', '~', navigate_to_cwd, { buffer = buf_id, desc = \"navigate to cwd\", })\r\n    end,\r\n  })\r\n...\r\n```\r\nBut this will open mini.files using the parent of current buffers as anchor. that's not what I want to do.\r\n\r\nwould it be possible to add a new function `MiniFiles.navigate_to_file` (or some more options to `MiniFiles.refresh`) that given a path would recursively \"go_out\" until `cwd` or a common root under cwd is found, and then \"go_in\" to the file path?  I'm not sure how complex this would be to add, so I understand if you don't want to add something like this.\r\n",
