            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI think what you describing is already present: [`@` will reveal current cwd](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/78a4d457718060fe80480c72a7d64f6b23472d63/doc/mini-files.txt#L163) with [`reveal_cwd()` being its functional alternative](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/78a4d457718060fe80480c72a7d64f6b23472d63/doc/mini-files.txt#L732).\r\n\r\nOpening explorer with the focus on current buffer file [has suggested solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/78a4d457718060fe80480c72a7d64f6b23472d63/doc/mini-files.txt#L633-L634). Yes, it uses file's directory as anchor, but together with `reveal_cwd` I think this should be enough.",
