            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It doesn't work very well for when I have changes in the mini.files buffer(need to sync before closing the existing mini.files buffer). but that's just a minor inconvenience.\r\n\r\nNot sure I am following. You don't have to sync when going outside of current 'mini.files' buffer (which is displayed inside a single pane). You can navigate inside same explorer as much as you want and sync only when you're done.\r\n\r\nFor example, you can move file from one directory to another by cutting corresponding entry in a buffer (with `dd`), navigating in the target directory, paste (with `P`), and sync (with `=`).",
