            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ... use `~` to go back to the directory of the file I opened for editing (to copy another file, etc..) mini.files asks,\r\n\r\nAh, yes. The thing here is that the function uses `MiniFiles.open()`, which is not really a \"navigate to\" but \"open an explorer at\". So it tries to close the current explorer (as there can be only one explorer per tabpage).\r\n\r\nExporting functions to \"navigate\" inside particular explorer is currently not a goal.",
